}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"bfeb73fd-76a9-463d-8cf1-7cbe551eabec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Definition: a walk ",
 StyleBox["v0", "TI"],
 ", \[Ellipsis], ",
 StyleBox["vk", "TI"],
 " is a geodesic at infra-scale ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 " when every window of ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 " consecutive vertices together with the next one is a shortest path: ",
 StyleBox["d(v(i\[Minus]s), vi) = s", "TI"],
 " for ",
 StyleBox["i \[GreaterEqual] s", "TI"],
 ", and ",
 StyleBox["d(v0, vi) = i", "TI"],
 " for ",
 StyleBox["i < s", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"bfa9a670-0e82-4dc1-b14f-675b7a7723ad"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The condition gets stronger as ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 " grows, so a walk that passes at ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 " passes at every smaller scale. The ladder is exact at both ends: at scale ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1e9afc4f-6f0f-4415-8210-66082834ccaf"],
 " the test is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraWalkQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraWalkQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "2cf8161f-4c9e-49d4-9c0a-dbae58eaa411"],
 ", at scale ",
 Cell[BoxData["Infinity"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "27ff43f0-cf97-48f1-8ba9-3aeb2e94a342"],
 " it is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraSegmentQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraSegmentQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ebfdbddf-0c82-4453-9152-e4d1abca8de7"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"9ed0fa21-e146-4731-b027-e55d3fdaa573"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["walk", "TI"],
 " may be a vertex list, a walk graph such as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["RandomInfraGeodesic"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/RandomInfraGeodesic", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "05bbdbb3-b23b-436d-9273-4a6f83bcc2bd"],
 " returns, a list of walk graphs, or a directed acyclic graph. A DAG passes \
when every path from a source to a sink passes, so the interval and spray \
graphs can be tested without listing their paths one by one. A walk of fewer \
than two vertices is not a geodesic."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"da1b7b25-159b-4204-a196-4766c31b94e0"]
}, Open  ]],

